'" roff
.TH litepkg 1 "May 1, 2026" "litepkg 1.0" "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
litepkg \- A simple tool for managing packages locally.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B litepkg
[
.B \-h
|
.BI \-v " VERSION"
]
[
.BI "COMMAND" " ARGUMENTS..."
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page describes the
.B litepkg
command, a utility for managing packages.
It allows users to list, install, and clean packages with ease.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all installed packages.
.TP
.B install
Install a new package. Requires package name as an argument.
.TP
.B clean
Clean up temporary build files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-h , \-\-help
Display this help message and exit.
.TP
.BI \-v , \-\-version " VERSION"
Output version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Example 1: List packages
.RS
.B litepkg
list
.RE
.TP
.B Example 2: Install a package
.RS
.B litepkg
install my-package
.RE
.TP
.B Example 3: Clean up
.RS
.B litepkg
clean
.RE
